WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.999
IEC 62443 is a family of standards focused on cybersecurity for industrial automation and control systems.

00:00:06.999 --> 00:00:11.742
These systems monitor or control physical processes in manufacturing, energy, water,

00:00:11.742 --> 00:00:14.329
transportation, buildings, and other operational environments.

00:00:14.329 --> 00:00:18.640
Their security must account for safety, availability, reliability, process integrity,

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.365
and long equipment lifecycles.

00:00:20.365 --> 00:00:27.264
The standards provide a structured way to discuss industrial cyber risk across organizations and technical disciplines.

00:00:27.264 --> 00:00:31.575
They address security programs, system design, risk assessment, product development,

00:00:31.575 --> 00:00:34.162
technical capabilities, integration, and service delivery.

00:00:34.162 --> 00:00:40.199
IEC 62443 is therefore broader than a list of firewall settings or product features.

00:00:40.199 --> 00:00:46.666
Asset owners use the concepts to establish governance and determine what protection their operations require.

00:00:46.666 --> 00:00:50.978
Integrators translate those requirements into an architecture and commissioned system.

00:00:50.978 --> 00:00:56.152
Product suppliers build security capabilities into components and maintain secure development practices.

00:00:56.152 --> 00:01:00.464
Service providers support systems without weakening the controls around them.

00:01:00.464 --> 00:01:06.500
This division of responsibility matters because no single product can secure an industrial operation.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.518
A capable component can be configured poorly.

00:01:09.518 --> 00:01:13.830
A well-segmented system can be exposed through unmanaged remote access.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:20.297
Strong policy can fail if teams cannot produce evidence that controls are implemented and maintained.

00:01:20.297 --> 00:01:23.747
IEC 62443 should be treated as a risk-based,

00:01:23.747 --> 00:01:25.903
lifecycle-oriented framework for disciplined engineering.

00:01:25.903 --> 00:01:30.645
It does not eliminate uncertainty or replace knowledge of the process.

00:01:30.645 --> 00:01:34.526
Its practical value comes from connecting organizational responsibility, architecture,

00:01:34.526 --> 00:01:35.819
technical requirements, verification,

00:01:35.819 --> 00:01:39.700
and ongoing operation using a common industrial cybersecurity language.
